\ connect.fam — connecting and disconnecting blocks (docs/NODE.md, steps 5
\ and 6), after state.fam and proofs.fam: tabminer's Chain::connect and
\ disconnect (miner/src/chain.rs).
\
\ stinit ( fd -- )  the state in the tree open as fd (genesis's, empty, if
\ new).
\ sconnect ( h body n -- code )  connects the block with header h and body
\ (n bytes) on the last one: 0, or the rule it breaks (tabminer's
\ ChainError, as fam_vectors.rs's state_code numbers them: -10 malformed,
\ -11 the body commitment, -12 too large, -13 an unknown input, -15 the
\ state root, -16 the supply, -17 the proof; -20 to -26 the name rules;
\ -30 to -35 the body's own).  A block refused changes nothing.  Its chain
\ proof is checked when sprchk is set (prinit first).
\ sconn1 ( h body n -- ) and sconn2 ( ok -- code )  sconnect in two:
\ everything to the chain proof's public values (ppub; spend set if the
\ proof is to be checked), then, given the verifier's verdict, the rest
\ (the store written, or the block refused); between them the store's
\ transaction is open, so nothing else may use the state.
\ sundo ( -- )  undoes the last block connected.
\ A block's body is kept for the last 1,008 blocks (tabminer's default
\ --max-undo-blocks): 'b', the height, the chunk (1 KiB each); its
\ length at chunk FFFF.

: sprchk variable ;  : bbody variable ;  : bbn variable ;
\ swk: if set, the block's header entry (headers.fam's: its id at CC, its
\ cumulative work at EC): its work kept with its header ('w', the height)
\ for a start to resume from the middle of the chain (sync.fam's nload),
\ and its height under its id ('i', the id's first 8 bytes), for old
\ headers found by id (query.fam's yfind; a stale one, of a block undone,
\ found not to match).
: swk variable ;
: kwork  kb @ 1 lit + 4 lit be!  77 lit kb @ c!  5 lit ;   \ ( height -- klen )
: kid  kb @ 1 lit + 8 lit bcopy  69 lit kb @ c!  9 lit ;   \ ( id -- klen )
\ shidx ( e -- )  entry e's work and id kept for its height (in the
\ transaction open).
: shidx
dup 20 lit + @ kwork  over EC lit + 20 lit sput
dup 20 lit + @ sbuf @ !  CC lit + kid sbuf @ 4 lit sput ;

\ The undo record's keys: 'u', the height, the chunk; the body's, 'b'.
: kundo  kb @ 5 lit + 2 lit be!  kb @ 1 lit + 4 lit be!  75 lit kb @ c!  7 lit ;   \ ( h chunk -- klen )
: kbody  kb @ 5 lit + 2 lit be!  kb @ 1 lit + 4 lit be!  62 lit kb @ c!  7 lit ;   \ ( h chunk -- klen )
\ bdrop ( h -- )  block h's body, if kept, dropped.
: bdrop
dup FFFF lit kbody sbuf @ 4 lit sget 4 lit = if
	sbuf @ @ 3FF lit + A lit rshift ?dup if 0 lit do dup i kbody sdel loop then
	FFFF lit kbody sdel
else drop then ;

: sroot0  srt !  27 lit 0 lit tmpa @ nget  tmpb @ troot  tmpa @ tmpb @ srt @ compress  srt @ dfrom ;   \ ( c -- )  in a transaction
: sroot  stfd @ 0 lit txbegin stx !  sroot0  stx @ txcommit drop ;

\ What connecting a block took, in ticks, by part: its body decoded and
\ its commitment checked (btb), the state changed and its root checked
\ (bts), its chain proof (btp), the store's writes and commit (btc).
: bt0 variable ;  : btb variable ;  : bts variable ;  : btp variable ;  : btc variable ;
: btick  ticks dup bt0 @ - rot ! bt0 ! ;          \ ( var -- )  the time since the last, into var

: spend variable ;  : stxo variable ;
: sconn1  ( h body n -- )
ticks bt0 !  0 lit rtn !  0 lit rtall !
rot bh !  2dup bbn ! bbody !  0 lit bcode !  0 lit ndirty !
2dup bparse nip
bcode @ 0= if stmd @ bcommit  stmd @ dfrom  stmd @ bh @ 2C lit + 8 lit wcmp if FFFFFFF5 lit bfail then then
bcode @ 0= if CC lit + 1E8480 lit u> if FFFFFFF4 lit bfail then else drop then
btb btick
0 lit stxo !  0 lit spend !
bcode @ 0= if
	stfd @ 1 lit txbegin stx !  1 lit stxo !
	bh @ 20 lit + @ sh !
	70 lit mget dup sctr ! sfirst !  71 lit mget dup sctrh ! sfirsth !
	bnin @ 3 lit lshift 400 lit + malloc dup ub ! ux !
	0 lit u,  sfirst @ u,  bnout @ u,  sfirsth @ u,  bnin @ u,
	spent @ 4 lit wzero  made @ 4 lit wzero
	\ the inputs spent
	bnin @ ?dup if 0 lit do bcode @ 0= if
		bin @ i 5 lit * + pos@  over u, dup u,
		2dup oget if
			sbuf @ 20 lit + slotamt spent @ amount+
			2dup kspent sbuf @ 44 lit sput
			odel
		else 2drop FFFFFFF3 lit bfail then
	then loop then
	\ the outputs added
	bcode @ 0= if bnout @ ?dup if 0 lit do
		bout @ i 3C lit * +  dup rb @ 34 lit bcopy
		34 lit + dup le@ swap 4 lit + le@
		2dup made @ amount+
		over 3FFFFFFF lit and rb @ 34 lit + !
		over 1E lit rshift over 2 lit lshift or 3FFFFFFF lit and rb @ 38 lit + !
		nip 1C lit rshift rb @ 3C lit + !
		sh @ rb @ 40 lit + !
		rb @ sctr @ sctrh @ oput  sinc
	loop then then
	bcode @ 0= if snames then
	bcode @ 0= if sprop  stmd @ sroot0  stmd @ bh @ 4C lit + 8 lit wcmp if FFFFFFF1 lit bfail then then
	\ the supply: what the outputs make, what the inputs held and the subsidy
	bcode @ 0= if sh @ subsidy spent @ amount+  made @ spent @ 4 lit wcmp if FFFFFFF0 lit bfail then then
	bts btick
	\ the proof, last (tabminer's order): its public values here, the
	\ verifier's verdict given to sconn2
	bcode @ 0= sprchk @ and if sstmt if 1 lit spend ! else FFFFFFEF lit bfail then then
then ;

: sconn2  ( ok -- code )
spend @ if 0= if FFFFFFEF lit bfail then else drop then
stxo @ if
	btp btick
	bcode @ 0= if
		ux @ ub @ - 2 lit rshift ub @ !
		ub @ @ 2 lit lshift urem !  ub @ up !  0 lit uk !
		begin urem @ while
			urem @ 400 lit u< if urem @ else 400 lit then
			sh @ uk @ kundo up @ 2 lit pick sput
			dup up @ + up !  urem @ swap - urem !  uk @ 1 lit + uk !
		repeat
		\ the body, kept for 1,008 blocks
		bbn @ sbuf @ !  sh @ FFFF lit kbody sbuf @ 4 lit sput
		\ the first body kept, once (meta 62: what our status says we hold
		\ from, sync.fam's nstat)
		62 lit mget 0= if sh @ 62 lit mput then
		bbody @ up !  bbn @ urem !  0 lit uk !
		begin urem @ while
			urem @ 400 lit u< if urem @ else 400 lit then
			sh @ uk @ kbody up @ 2 lit pick sput
			dup up @ + up !  urem @ swap - urem !  uk @ 1 lit + uk !
		repeat
		sh @ 3F0 lit u> if sh @ 3F0 lit - bdrop then
		\ the snapshot after it, to serve (manifest.fam), for as long
		mbuckets  msoff @ 0= if sh @ sctr @ sctrh @ msnap  sh @ 3F0 lit u> if sh @ 3F0 lit - mdrop then then
		sctr @ 70 lit mput  sctrh @ 71 lit mput  sh @ 68 lit mput  sh @ khdr bh @ CC lit sput
		swk @ ?dup if shidx then
		serr @ if FFFFFFF6 lit bfail then
	then
	bcode @ if stx @ txabort drop 0 lit ndirty ! else stx @ txcommit drop then
	btc btick
	ub @ free
then
bops @ free
bcode @ ;

: sconnect  ( h body n -- code )  sconn1  spend @ if ppub @ bpr @ bnpr @ cvverify else -1 lit then  sconn2 ;

\ uevent ( p -- )  undoes one event of the names section.
: uevent
dup @
dup 1 lit = if drop
	4 lit + dup @ swap 4 lit + dup @ swap 4 lit +
	dup dup 20 lit + @ stmd @ cleaf  stmd @ dfrom
	stmd @ rb @ 8 lit wcopy  dup 24 lit + rb @ 20 lit + 8 lit wcopy  dup 20 lit + @ rb @ 40 lit + !
	-rot 2dup rb @ -rot oput
	kcommit swap 24 lit sput
else dup 2 lit = if drop
	4 lit + dup rtouch  dup krec sdel  tremove
else 3 lit = if
	4 lit + dup @ swap 4 lit + swap
	over nlv2 @ rvalue  nkey @ tk2 @ 4 lit wcopy  tk2 @ nlv2 @ tupdate
	tk2 @ krec -rot sput  tk2 @ rtouch
else drop then then then ;

: sundo
stfd @ 1 lit txbegin stx !
68 lit mget sh !
sh @ 0 lit kundo sbuf @ 400 lit sget drop
sbuf @ @ 2 lit lshift dup malloc dup ub ! up ! urem !
0 lit uk !
begin urem @ while
	sh @ uk @ kundo up @ 400 lit sget  dup up @ + up !  urem @ swap - urem !  uk @ 1 lit + uk !
repeat
ub @ 4 lit + @ sfirst !  ub @ C lit + @ sfirsth !  70 lit mget sctr !  71 lit mget sctrh !
\ the block's outputs and commits leave
\ (40-bit positions, from sfirst, as many as the counter passed)
sfirst @ sfirsth @  sctr @ sfirst @ -  ?dup if 0 lit do
	2dup odel  2dup kcommit sdel
	swap 1 lit + dup 0= if swap 1 lit + else swap then
loop then 2drop
\ the inputs return
ub @ 10 lit + @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	ub @ 14 lit + i 3 lit lshift + dup @ swap 4 lit + @
	2dup kspent sbuf @ 44 lit sget drop
	2dup sbuf @ -rot oput
	kspent sdel
loop then
\ the names section, last event first
ub @ 14 lit + ub @ 10 lit + @ 3 lit lshift +
0 lit nev !
begin dup ub @ ub @ @ 2 lit lshift + u< while
	dup ev @ nev @ w!  nev @ 1 lit + nev !
	dup @ dup 1 lit = if drop 50 lit else dup 2 lit = if drop 14 lit else 3 lit = if 8C lit else 4 lit then then then +
repeat drop
nev @ ?dup if 0 lit do ev @ nev @ 1 lit - i - w@ uevent loop then
sfirst @ 70 lit mput  sfirsth @ 71 lit mput  sh @ 1 lit - 68 lit mput
62 lit mget sh @ = if 0 lit 62 lit mput then  sh @ khdr sdel  sh @ kwork sdel  sh @ bdrop  sh @ mdrop
ub @ @ 2 lit lshift 3FF lit + A lit rshift 0 lit do sh @ i kundo sdel loop
mbuckets
sprop
stx @ txcommit drop
ub @ free ;

: stinit  ( fd -- )
stfd !  p2init dvinit
100 lit alloc kb !  100 lit alloc kb2 !  400 lit alloc sbuf !  400 lit alloc rtb !  0 lit rtn !  0 lit rtall !  minit
520 lit alloc dflt !  2000 lit alloc lvs !
20 lit alloc tmpa !  20 lit alloc tmpb !  20 lit alloc stmd !
10000 lit alloc dirty !  0 lit ndirty !
54 lit alloc tnb !  54 lit alloc tnode !  54 lit alloc toth !
10 lit alloc tkp !  10 lit alloc tkq !  10 lit alloc tz !  10 lit alloc tmpk !
40 lit alloc tha !  40 lit alloc thb !
80 lit alloc nel !  80 lit alloc nin !  10 lit alloc nkey !  60 lit alloc ob !
44 lit alloc rb !  24 lit alloc cb !
10 lit alloc spent !  10 lit alloc made !  10 lit alloc sw4 !
100 lit alloc ev !  10 lit alloc tk2 !  20 lit alloc nlv2 !
tz @ 4 lit wzero  dflt @ 8 lit wzero
28 lit 0 lit do i dfl i dfl i 1 lit + dfl compress loop
0 lit serr ! ;
